---
code: mark-standalone-rc-consumer
when-fires: the new-grammar mark parser found a standalone mark-block (no command to bind) carrying an rc-consumer or `reads`. oracle/predict/mark_grammar.rs.
why: 28A:rul-continuation-attachment: a standalone block has no statement to measure/back, so a verdict/observe there is unbacked ⇒ the block drops to ⊤ (`inv-top-reject`).
edit-loop: edit a sentence in the transcript below, then run `mise run loom:compile -- mark-standalone-rc-consumer && mise run loom:promote -- mark-standalone-rc-consumer`; prove it stuck with `mise run test`, which is also what catches anything else the promotion moved. `mise run loom:vars -- --all mark-standalone-rc-consumer` lists this case's values; type {{name}} to insert or move one.
